Day 55 — Read-only HTTP/UI observation
Target: https://hack-yourself-first.com/Supercar/7
Observed: 2026-10-26 20:16 +05:30

Request
GET /Supercar/7 HTTP/2
Host: hack-yourself-first.com

Response metadata
HTTP/2 200
content-type: text/html; charset=utf-8
cache-control: private
x-xss-protection: 0
x-aspnetmvc-version: 5.1

UI observation
Opening the vehicle details page in the browser produced a native JavaScript
alert ("81317") during page rendering and blocked access to the page until the
dialog is handled. The response is server-rendered HTML, not a JSON API.
The page includes a community comments section. The response body and comment
contents are intentionally not reproduced here.

Reproduction
1. Send the read-only GET request above in a browser.
2. Observe the unexpected blocking browser alert during rendering.

Scope / safety
No form submission, state change, payload replay, or external request was
performed. A separate GET with the response body discarded confirmed the
HTTP status and metadata above. Stop further testing unless explicitly
authorized.
